{
  "version": 1,
  "meta": {
    "name": "jamba-v0.1",
    "family": "jamba",
    "notes": "Mamba-1 and attention in one stack, with a mixture of experts on every other layer. Two periods run at once: attention appears every eighth layer at offset four, and a mixture on every odd layer, so the repeating unit is eight layers and thirty-two is four of them. Only four of the thirty-two layers hold a cache that grows with the sequence; the other twenty-eight carry a state fixed per sequence, which is why a 256k context costs so little to hold. There is no positional embedding anywhere: the state-space layers carry the order, so the attention layers need none.",
    "published": {
      "params": 51570323328,
      "source": "https://huggingface.co/ai21labs/Jamba-v0.1"
    }
  },
